#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1200.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499598} :activity/id #uuid "37d9328b-f5cc-5af8-87e2-f52cd07d5248" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048840 :topic/id #uuid "c53ff2b5-bc81-56fe-a0dc-0336484fb64d" :topic/math-academy-id 555} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499581 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499434 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499457 :question/id #uuid "392a598d-d5a4-555b-96d5-3e6125a3b2b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-2283"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01f99115-f376-50c2-9b7e-79800006d437" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499459} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499472} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499501} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499513} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499545} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534078} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534092} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558539} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558540}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value Given a Ratio by Rounding an Amount"} :step/id #uuid "3990eff7-9439-5ea7-a839-81c63a117a93" :step/math-academy-id 648009 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499582}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499582 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499440 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499464 :question/id #uuid "43fbc756-3ac8-517b-a6c5-99ae38b706c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-2284"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a02676df-7c77-5303-9d8e-7c83fdfd2060" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499480} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499525} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499541} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499550} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499551} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534068} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558491} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558561}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios"} :step/id #uuid "39d2b0a2-a796-5c2d-87be-ef9b250b51be" :step/math-academy-id 648012} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499441 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499450 :question/id #uuid "23152915-ce5d-502c-9347-c4889b9103df" :question/math-academy-id "e-2282"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c71ff81f-388d-53c8-853e-c60430327148" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499448} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499499} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499526} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499531} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534035} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534069} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558515}] :knowledge-point/title "Approximating Ratios by Rounding to the Nearest Hundred"} :step/id #uuid "64bb8dc3-c0c9-5342-9899-e92b00265817" :step/math-academy-id 648005 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499607}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499598 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499639 :tutorial/content "We can use what we know about rounding numbers to approximate ratios.\nWe round the quantities to a given degree first, before setting up the ratio.\n\nLook at the following table, which shows the number of girls in a ballet school with blonde or black hair.\n\n| Blonde Hair | Black Hair |\n| --- | --- |\n| $33$ | $58$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest ten, let's determine the approximate ratio of girls with blonde hair to girls with black hair.\n\nFirst, let's approximate the number of girls with blonde or black hair by rounding to the nearest ten.\n\n- Number of girls with blonde hair: $33 \\longrightarrow 30$\n\n- Number of girls with black hair: $58 \\longrightarrow 60$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of girls with blonde hair to the number of girls with black hair is approximately\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{30}{60}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{30 \\div 10}{60 \\div 10} = \\dfrac{3}{6}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of girls with blonde hair to the number of girls with black hair is approximately $\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "777fe794-e3cc-5250-a9e8-e407cc3f306c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2052 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "805b138d-9de3-5c18-96bd-507752cfcb3d" :step/math-academy-id 648000 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499607 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499634 :tutorial/content "Now, let's see how we can find a value given the ratio and another value.\n\nSuppose at a school library, there are some science books and $396$ history books. The ratio of the number of science books to the number of history books is $3: 4.$ By rounding the number of history books to the nearest ten, approximate the number of science books in the library.\n\nFirst, let's approximate the number of history books:\n\n$$\n396 \\longrightarrow 400\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the number of science books to the number of history books is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nHere, \n\n- the numerator represents the number of science books, and\n\n- the denominator represents the number of history books.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $400$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $100{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 \\times 100}{4 \\times 100} = \\dfrac{300}{400}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $300$ science books in the library." :tutorial/id #uuid "16e103a1-de00-5acb-9566-24168dec17eb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14923 :tutorial/title "Finding a Value Given a Ratio"} :step/id #uuid "9d54fdb2-7a7b-5fda-81dd-61e03fb3fa56" :step/math-academy-id 648008 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499581}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499610 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499435 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499520 :question/id #uuid "a8368c62-f936-54c5-b069-1adabcb11ffe" :question/math-academy-id "e-2281"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10523576-ab54-5731-bfaf-999a591295e0" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499456} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499477} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499530} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499559}] :knowledge-point/title "Approximating Ratios by Rounding to the Nearest Ten"} :step/id #uuid "aa6626df-e1ca-57ff-8e3c-685699ee9c0c" :step/math-academy-id 648001 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499591}}] :activity/title "Approximating Ratios" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498720}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534139} :activity/id #uuid "09a164ce-ad3d-58c3-9305-a48a254fe99f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048840 :topic/id #uuid "c53ff2b5-bc81-56fe-a0dc-0336484fb64d" :topic/math-academy-id 555} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534126 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3f15eb-c686-501d-80b8-1f41855dcc40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533165} {:answer/id #uuid "1c515615-ec9e-5ba1-8ca1-601c55e23e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$6$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533207} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9d41c5-7037-5cd7-aa0c-6d98056a697a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533252} {:answer/id #uuid "c9360364-ef93-5795-aaa0-0811fa98160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533620} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c87a01-7ace-5e64-a20d-4355299a734e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$15$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533749}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533207} :answer-field/id #uuid "69d68b6c-b19c-5342-87f0-f1a951317aa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f65ffc41-5bca-5c7e-a470-b626911bf2cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-93113" :question/problem "Samantha and Harry each bought a watermelon. The ratio of the weight of Samantha's watermelon to the weight of Harry's watermelon is $5:3.$ Samantha's watermelon weighs $12$ kilograms. By rounding this weight to the nearest ten, approximate the weight of Harry's watermelon." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the weight of Samantha's watermelon to the nearest ten:\n\n$$\n12⟶10\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the weight of Samantha's watermelon to the weight of Harry's watermelon is \n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the weight of Samantha's  watermelon and the denominator represents  the weight of Harry's watermelon.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $10$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 2}{3\\times 2}=\\frac{10}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Harry's watermelon approximately weighs $6$ kilograms."} :step/id #uuid "5ae6fd03-7d26-5fc4-8d37-964087984c67" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534147}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534139 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02603c07-dd10-5687-84ae-5f4c0be4ab2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533136} {:answer/id #uuid "28a8ea65-0785-5201-bbdf-14a3661d4e5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533241} {:answer/id #uuid "3c64e603-d081-5cb3-9278-c26a4ab3e27e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533280} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca4d6ec-255a-5d79-af66-de6061ebddfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533392} {:answer/id #uuid "7525cca7-6301-5a3f-84e3-2eb780c2eb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533417}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533417} :answer-field/id #uuid "69081031-c0ac-5dc2-9f83-909e212c6666" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cceba1db-cf64-5613-ace7-49dabd9ac195" :question/math-academy-id "q-93076" :question/problem "Only apple and cherry trees grow in a garden. The following table shows the number of these trees.\n\n| Apple trees | Cherry trees |\n| --- | --- |\n| $271$ | $425$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the number of apple trees to the total number of trees." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the number of apple and cherry trees by rounding to the nearest hundred.\n\n- Apple trees: $271⟶300$\n\n- Cherry trees: $425⟶400$\n\nThus, the total number of trees is approximately $300+400=700.$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of apple trees to the total number of trees (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{300}{700}.\n$$\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $100$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{300÷100}{700÷100}=\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of apple trees to the total number of trees is approximately $\\frac{3}{7}.$"} :step/id #uuid "a099c9b4-d1ce-5863-8969-e24fe375544d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534157}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534145 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c08cff7-c809-5121-b744-11d3019f8279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533163} {:answer/id #uuid "c06d78f0-10b4-518d-8220-6a66d562d55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533604} {:answer/id #uuid "ce7add3f-d5d9-5c37-a278-9620c6062894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533640} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c04c8e-bd71-5713-91f5-1e65209c705d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533654} {:answer/id #uuid "f23155c7-a1e2-5198-af78-7d8df533c0b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533734}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533654} :answer-field/id #uuid "94410187-a34e-500a-81d7-ff4c37da8f94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "987f037f-66db-5b9e-acaa-f2176b3629c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-349588" :question/problem "Only orange and peach trees grow in a garden. The following table shows the number of these trees.\n\n| Orange trees | Peach trees |\n| --- | --- |\n| $352$ | $618$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the number of orange trees to the total number of trees." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the number of orange and peach trees by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- Orange trees: $352⟶400$\n\n- Peach trees: $618⟶600$\n\nThus, the total number of trees is approximately $400+600=1\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of orange trees to the total number of trees is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{400}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{400÷100}{1\\,000÷100}=\\frac{4}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of orange trees to the total number of trees is approximately $\\frac{2}{5}.$"} :step/id #uuid "b89d46db-aacc-5300-81b4-f42199193213"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534147 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cdd9f1-49bc-529f-9cf3-7d15b171045a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$180$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533340} {:answer/id #uuid "72bffca4-ed36-5955-afe3-b6ce9cb972ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$125$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533413} {:answer/id #uuid "890baf66-3b7c-5d6b-a240-4e42025caf2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$200$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533467} {:answer/id #uuid "93031dca-4a2f-590b-b511-f9479c81542f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$160$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533493} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b144a7-2a2a-5401-8855-dfc1a8d02933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$130$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533733}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533467} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a8f5b83-2a82-5f6e-95fd-274ba7bd818d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc81aa2c-a8cb-5dba-82e1-77d0c6319f70" :question/math-academy-id "q-93267" :question/problem "The following table shows the amount, in grams, of flax oil obtained from the corresponding amount of flaxseed:\n\n| Oil | Seed |\n| --- | --- |\n| $315$ | $945$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the amount of flax oil to the amount of flaxseed is always the same. By rounding the given data to the nearest hundred, approximate the amount of flax oil that can be obtained from $600$ grams of seed." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the amounts of flax oil and seed:\n\n- Oil: $315⟶300$\n\n- Seed: $945⟶900$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the amount of flax oil to the amount of flaxseed (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{300}{900}.\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the amount of flax oil and the denominator represents the amount of flaxseed.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{300÷100}{900÷100}=\\frac{3}{9}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3÷3}{9÷3}=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $600$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $200$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 200}{3\\times 200}=\\frac{200}{600}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $200$ grams of flax oil can be obtained from $600$ grams of flaxseed."} :step/id #uuid "bf26c5b2-fa41-5f58-9926-3debfa64da79" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534145}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534157 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25cb37b5-2d4e-5670-bd41-bb1e65a2f188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533235} {:answer/id #uuid "28656814-767a-5b15-91aa-42642f0f926b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533239} {:answer/id #uuid "3b73f981-baed-51be-bc72-ae388cf830f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533278} {:answer/id #uuid "5dffe28d-f55c-57d9-a24f-952a67152c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533354} {:answer/id #uuid "a3cdbf4a-9fd3-52b6-ba6f-df93bb7df832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533535}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533278} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d04ac50-0af2-5115-b945-5c001afd6b25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de53ade3-2006-5489-a226-17f2c3957439" :question/math-academy-id "q-93112" :question/problem "There are $98$ blue marbles and some red marbles in a box. The ratio of the number of blue marbles to the number of red ones is $2:1.$ By rounding the number of blue marbles to the nearest ten, approximate the number of red marbles in the box." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the number of blue marbles:\n\n$$\n98⟶100\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the number of blue marbles to the number of red marbles is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the number of blue marbles and the denominator represents the number of red marbles.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $100$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $50:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 50}{1\\times 50}=\\frac{100}{50}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $50$ red marbles in the box."} :step/id #uuid "efa27ae5-ad45-5b59-a5b8-4d12f16c5865" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534126}}] :activity/title "Approximating Ratios" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533118}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558589} :activity/id #uuid "3d8d5793-d336-5605-bbdc-d6f9f23c2473" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048840 :topic/id #uuid "c53ff2b5-bc81-56fe-a0dc-0336484fb64d" :topic/math-academy-id 555} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558515 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d823593-d438-5d97-8b01-142529984e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558047} {:answer/id #uuid "9a744675-7473-5107-89cd-7f5bda0b2c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558166} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a1d657-a365-52a6-93bd-7432c4dc6cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558219} {:answer/id #uuid "c8118063-eee9-5ee4-95c2-103ff9c67e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558266} {:answer/id #uuid "dda00e49-ce3c-5659-ba54-882d075f24ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558219} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddd74be-973a-5825-bb01-179a7478c7d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4f394066-5fc4-5966-8c8c-7e49bac1b23a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93064" :question/problem "The following table shows the width and length,  in meters, of a rectangular agriculture field.\n\n| Width | Length |\n| --- | --- |\n| $667$ | $1\\,432$ |\n\nRounding to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of width to length for this field." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the width and length by rounding to the nearest $100$:\n\n- width: $667⟶700$\n\n- length: $1\\,432⟶1\\,400$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of width to length is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{700}{1\\,400}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{700÷100}{1\\,400÷100}=\\frac{7}{14}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7÷7}{14÷7}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of width to length is approximately $\\frac{1}{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "16aae4ea-1ad8-5274-96f3-862ce4f5ef5f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558619}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558619 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06919843-5a8b-5259-9299-09b587346303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$300$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557884} {:answer/id #uuid "1007f262-7909-5942-b76a-6cedb12bc50f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$250$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557900} {:answer/id #uuid "568cf1d0-2c6f-5140-b128-a52b31b4c1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$200$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558029} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd745a4-5e02-5a78-9cf9-9af54448a980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$400$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558076} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8242bf-e0b6-5d87-afa2-323f38a9d5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$350$ kilograms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558305}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558029} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b374f4-e768-52a0-9c29-d75461c01b9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "132a5e4f-2931-5c22-94d5-e6d628c0a5d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-93081" :question/problem "The weight of ore and the weight of copper obtained from it, in kilograms, is shown in the following table:\n\n| Ore | Copper |\n| --- | --- |\n| $423$ | $68$ |\n\nThe ratio of the weight of ore to the weight of copper is always the same.  By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the weight of copper that can be obtained from $1\\,200$ kilograms of ore." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the weights of ore and copper:\n\n- Ore: $423⟶420$\n\n- Copper: $68⟶70$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of ore to copper (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{420}{70}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the weight of ore, and the denominator represents the weight of copper.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{420÷10}{70÷10}=\\frac{42}{7}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{42÷7}{7÷7}=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $1\\,200$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $200$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 200}{1\\times 200}=\\frac{1\\,200}{200}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $200$ kilograms of copper can be obtained from $1\\,200$ kilograms of ore."} :step/id #uuid "4ac6e817-f199-5922-9e9d-be3655e4c1c8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558634}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558634 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3615741b-46a4-5227-b3d1-750afe938f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$350$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557977} {:answer/id #uuid "60e762ea-1c99-5415-9c61-1cb6553b4b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$400$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558052} {:answer/id #uuid "61007c72-a194-5bd7-9737-2ab6110d4866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$450$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558053} {:answer/id #uuid "642d5471-d8d0-5f30-b841-f9ddb78ad020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$300$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558060} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb2834b-2c4a-5de7-a43c-ec0d2aebeaa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$250$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558060} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c802e76-90be-5a83-ad3b-13ee92d8dca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9587827d-60b3-5a55-a4d3-895d1d528b37" :question/math-academy-id "q-93115" :question/problem "Grant and Stephanie ate a whole cake together. The ratio of the amount of cake eaten by Grant to the amount of cake eaten by Stephanie is $7:3.$ Grant ate $745$ grams of cake. By rounding this weight to the nearest hundred, approximate the weight of Stephanie's portion." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the weight of the cake Grant ate to the nearest hundred:\n\n$$\n745⟶700\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the weight of Grant's portion to the weight of Stephanie's portion is \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the weight of Grant's  part and the denominator represents  the weight of Stephanies part.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $700$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $100:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 100}{3\\times 100}=\\frac{700}{300}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Stephanie ate approximately $300$ grams of cake."} :step/id #uuid "69ee0c21-c1b2-583d-b271-f07238247567" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558686}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022a4a93-f3c4-5aee-abd1-90bc3255912b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$16$ tablets" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557873} {:answer/id #uuid "3d704850-2838-563c-aef8-e418a2b3c148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$20$ tablets" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557993} {:answer/id #uuid "8e38cfb0-b6b5-576f-8f18-ac6fe927d170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$25$ tablets" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558144} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f809e8-955b-5304-81e5-e3dc3285884c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$30$ tablets" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558259} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a0f6ae-38cb-5459-b690-6d6809dc0a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$15$ tablets" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558316}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557993} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db6ae51-1959-57ad-8dff-d3275311dd80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c4649cc4-2caa-54b1-a9d4-13acf6f413f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-364172" :question/problem "The number of laptops and tablets in store A is shown in the following table:\n\n| Laptops | Tablets |\n| --- | --- |\n| $72$ | $38$ |\n\nIn store B there are approximately $35$ laptops. The ratio of the number of laptops to the number of tablets in both stores is the same. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of tablets in store B." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of laptops and tablets in store A:\n\n- Laptops: $72⟶70$\n\n- Tablets: $38⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of laptops to the number of tablets (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70}{40}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of laptops and the denominator represents the number of tablets.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $35$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $20$ tablets in store B."} :step/id #uuid "98230e05-80da-500f-9b67-ad4b98606748"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558686 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3753fd0b-c081-5341-ae6b-6434522711ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$900$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557978} {:answer/id #uuid "45d235ac-7712-5ca4-877d-63407f23d444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$600$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558006} {:answer/id #uuid "5b98ffd4-63ed-5add-bf98-ecf5d6492c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$760$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558042} {:answer/id #uuid "807be663-7835-5fd3-82ec-350b159ded0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$700$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558117} {:answer/id #uuid "881d6191-65af-5d92-988e-e00ce240a7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$840$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558006} :answer-field/id #uuid "0db908f9-7a3a-5a7e-a3ec-6a328a11d897" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "92ab7ff7-d02e-5687-bfb0-2e6e2beec2cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-364163" :question/problem "Maya and Leon get paid for painting houses. The ratio of Maya's reward to Leon's reward is $3:4.$ \nDuring a particular week, Leon received $$806.$ By rounding Leon's earnings to the nearest hundred, approximate the amount of money that Maya received." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the amount of money that Leon received:\n\n$$\n$806⟶$800\n$$\n\nThe ratio of Maya's earnings to Leon's earnings is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents Maya's earnings  and the denominator represents Leon's earnings.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $800$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $200$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 200}{4\\times 200}=\\frac{600}{800}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Maya received approximately $$600.$"} :step/id #uuid "cba98600-887f-500a-b3d4-907fdab73e5e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558661}}] :activity/title "Approximating Ratios" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557857}]}
